# Tailwind Class Conventions

Use named utilities from the Tailwind theme when the value exists on the scale. Reserve `[...]` arbitrary syntax for values with no matching utility.

## Prefer theme utilities

```tsx
// Avoid
className="lg:h-[4.5rem] lg:size-[1.125rem] p-[12px]"

// Prefer
className="lg:h-18 lg:size-4.5 p-3"
```

Check editor hints (`suggestCanonicalClasses`) before writing an arbitrary value.

## When arbitrary values are appropriate

- CSS variables: `grid-cols-[var(--app-sidebar-width)_minmax(0,1fr)]`
- Complex expressions: `w-[min(320px,calc(100vw-2rem))]`
- Properties without a utility: `transition-[grid-template-columns]`
- Values off the scale with no close match (e.g. a one-off 360px column)

## Reused off-scale values

If the same non-scale value appears more than once, add it to `@theme` in `client/styles/app.css` instead of repeating `[...]` literals.

```css
@theme inline {
  --width-login-form: 360px;
}
```

```tsx
className="lg:grid-cols-[1fr_var(--width-login-form)]"
```

## Generated UI primitives

Shadcn/Radix components may keep precise arbitrary math for third-party alignment. Do not rewrite those unless fixing a lint warning or the value maps cleanly to the theme.
